<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    decbench: kuna drops every stack-passed call argument at a call site whose
    callee prototype is unlocked.  Cases:
      O0-mydoom-mydoom-msg_b64enc                          (i386 PE)
      O2-noinline-openssh-portable-ssh-add-parse_dest_constraint (x86-64)

    Source (gcc -O2 -no-pie), reduced to the two functions below:

        __attribute__((noinline)) long callee(long a,long b,long c,long d,
                                              long e,long f,long h,long i)
        { return a+b+c+d+e+f+h*3+i*5; }
        __attribute__((noinline)) long caller(long x,long y)
        { return callee(1,2,3,4,5,6,x,y); }

    Under SysV x86-64 the first six arguments go in RDI/RSI/RDX/RCX/R8/R9 and
    arguments 7 and 8 are pushed on the stack; gcc emits the `push` form:

        1150 caller:   endbr64 ; push %rsi ; mov $6,%r9d ; mov $5,%r8d
                       mov $4,%ecx ; push %rdi ; mov $3,%edx ; mov $2,%esi
                       mov $1,%edi ; call 1120 (callee) ; pop %rdx ; pop %rcx ; ret

    Root cause (P4, active-input trial scoring).  Heritage::guard_calls DOES
    register a stack-parameter trial for each outgoing-argument slot and DOES
    append the argument Varnode to the CALL op.  One pass later,
    check_input_trial_use asks whether the slot lies inside the CALLER's own
    local stack range.  Upstream asks that of the argument Varnode's address
    (fspec.cc:5618, inRange(vn->getAddr(),1)); kuna asked it of the TRIAL's
    address.  guard_calls registers the trial at the callee-relative address
    (addr minus stackoffset) while creating the Varnode at the caller-relative one,
    so on a downward-growing stack the trial offsets are always positive
    (8, 16, 24, ...) and the caller's localrange is negative: every stack trial
    failed and was scored no-use.  A definitely-unused trial then has its CALL
    input replaced with constant 0, which hands the argument-producing
    computation to dead-code elimination. In the two decbench cases that deletes
    a whole for(;;) loop and a four-way ternary cascade respectively.

    Stage model: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring".  The P0 assertion
    `option callsitestackargs on|off` (default ON, upstream-faithful) selects
    which address the localrange test probes.

    Pass 1 (option callsitestackargs off) reproduces the bug: the call truncates
    at the six register arguments, and caller's own parameters x/y vanish as
    collateral because their only consumers were the two dropped arguments.
    Pass 2 (option callsitestackargs on, the default) proves the fix: both stack
    arguments are recovered and caller regains its two parameters.
-->
